package com.linguapro.android

object ScenarioBankC2 {
    private fun s(n: Int, text: String, a: ScenarioQuestion, b: ScenarioQuestion, transfer: String, c: ScenarioQuestion) =
        UnitScenario("C2-U$n", text, a, b, transfer, c)
    val items = listOf(
        s(1, "The director insisted that the company was merely tightening its belt. Mara glanced at the list of closed departments and replied that the belt appeared to have taken several people with it. Nobody mistook her remark for a discussion of clothing. Its force lay in extending the director's own metaphor until the reassuring phrase could no longer conceal the consequences. Later, a colleague urged her not to burn her bridges. She agreed to keep the meeting civil, but rejected the suggestion that civility required endorsing the description of the cuts. The exchange distinguishes preserving professional relationships from accepting a euphemism. Neither the director's idiom nor Mara's sharp response supplies a full account of the decision; each reveals a stance towards it that a literal summary alone would miss.",
            sq("What gives Mara's reply its critical force?", "She extends the reassuring metaphor to expose its human cost.", "She asks for a literal explanation of clothing.", "She endorses the cuts without qualification.", "Aynı kemer mecazını insan kaybına taşıyarak rahatlatıcı ifadeyi eleştiriyor."),
            sq("What distinction does Mara preserve?", "Civility does not require agreement with the euphemism.", "Professional relationships require approving every description.", "A sharp remark proves the full economic case.", "Keep meeting civil ile reject endorsing description birlikte korunuyor."),
            "The manager calls the closures 'a trim'; an employee asks why the trim has removed whole teams.",
            sq("What is the employee challenging?", "The minimising frame of the description", "The spelling of the word trim", "The existence of any team", "Küçük kesinti çağrışımı, bütün ekiplerin çıkarılmasıyla karşılaştırılarak sorgulanır.")),
        s(2, "Jon gave his colleague the benefit of the doubt when the first deadline was missed. A second delay, however, prompted him to ask for an explanation rather than repeat the same reassuring assumption. He had no proof of bad faith, but neither did uncertainty oblige him to suspend practical judgement indefinitely. The subsequent review uncovered a staffing problem that both parties had underestimated. They came to terms with the need to change the timetable, while acknowledging that the delay had exposed a deeper weakness in planning. Calling the episode a blessing in disguise captured the eventual opportunity to improve the process, but it did not erase the cost already borne by the customer. The account therefore uses idioms to mark changes in judgement, without allowing the positive ending to retroactively make every consequence beneficial.",
            sq("What does the positive ending not justify?", "Treating all earlier consequences as beneficial", "Recognising an opportunity to improve", "Revising the timetable", "Blessing in disguise sonraki fırsatı belirtse de müşterinin önceki maliyetini silmez."),
            sq("Why does Jon seek an explanation after the second delay?", "Uncertainty does not require indefinite suspension of judgement.", "He has conclusive proof of malicious intent.", "The first deadline was met perfectly.", "Bad faith kanıtlanmıyor; yine de tekrar eden gecikme pratik inceleme gerektiriyor."),
            "The setback eventually led to improvement, but people had already borne real costs.",
            sq("Which summary preserves the qualification?", "A later benefit does not erase earlier costs.", "The setback was beneficial in every respect.", "No improvement followed.", "Eventually ile already, olumlu sonucun önceki bedeli yok etmediğini gösterir.")),
        s(3, "The ceremonial notice declared that the committee would henceforth receive applications through a single portal. In an internal message, the same instruction became a plain request to use the new form from Monday. Both versions referred to the same change, but they positioned the reader differently: the notice invoked institutional authority, whereas the message foregrounded the action required. An editor removed forthwith from a further draft because it sounded immediate yet did not specify whether the writer meant the same day or the next working day. Formal diction could signal seriousness without resolving that ambiguity. The final notice retained its institutional register while adding an explicit start date. The exercise in register was therefore not a contest between grand language and simple language; it was an examination of what each choice conveyed and what still needed to be stated.",
            sq("What did the formal wording fail to resolve by itself?", "The precise timing of the instruction", "Whether a committee existed", "The portal's colour", "Forthwith aciliyet tonu taşıyor, fakat somut gün ve çalışma günü sınırını açıklamıyordu."),
            sq("How do the two registers position the reader differently?", "One invokes authority; the other foregrounds the required action.", "They necessarily describe different factual changes.", "One proves compliance without action.", "Institutional authority ile action required, aynı olgunun farklı sunumudur."),
            "The notice says 'henceforth', then adds 'from Monday' to make the start date explicit.",
            sq("What does the added phrase contribute?", "Operational precision alongside formal register", "A contradiction of every instruction", "A promise of legal validity", "From Monday somut başlangıç sağlar; örnek metin hukuki geçerlilik iddiası taşımaz.")),
        s(4, "The review described the narrator's curiosity as childlike, but dismissed his response to criticism as childish. The shared reference to childhood did not make the adjectives interchangeable: one preserved a sense of openness, while the other evaluated the reaction as immature. Elsewhere, the reviewer distinguished continual interruptions from a continuous background hum, using the first for recurring disruptions and the second for an unbroken sound. These distinctions were not decorative displays of vocabulary. They shaped how the reader pictured both character and setting. Replacing every term with a broadly similar synonym would have blurred the evaluations and temporal patterns on which the interpretation depended. Precision emerged from selecting the word whose connotations and conditions fitted the passage, rather than from assuming that a rarer word would always be a better one.",
            sq("What distinguishes 'childlike' from 'childish' here?", "Openness is contrasted with an immature reaction.", "Both carry exactly the same evaluation.", "Neither refers to any behaviour.", "Curiosity olumlu açıklık; criticism response olgunlaşmamış tepki olarak değerlendiriliyor."),
            sq("What temporal contrast is made?", "Recurring interruptions versus an unbroken hum", "Two identical uninterrupted sounds", "A hum that never exists", "Continual tekrarlayan, continuous kesintisiz örneklerle kullanılmıştır."),
            "The noise is continuous, but the interruptions are continual: they happen repeatedly with gaps.",
            sq("Which distinction is intended?", "Unbroken duration versus recurrence", "Loudness versus silence only", "Two perfectly synonymous temporal descriptions", "With gaps ifadesi, tekrarın kesintisiz süreklilikten ayrıldığını gösterir.")),
        s(5, "The article proposed a new framework and described the findings as corroborating its central account. The discussion nevertheless included a caveat: the cases had been selected from institutions already interested in reform, so the framework's reach beyond that setting remained uncertain. A commentator treated the caveat as an admission that the entire argument had collapsed. Another reader took the opposite shortcut and ignored it because the main findings were supportive. Neither reading respected the structure of the claim. Corroboration can increase support for an account without establishing unrestricted applicability; a caveat can delimit an inference without nullifying every observation. A rigorous response would ask which parts of the argument the evidence strengthens, which alternatives remain plausible, and which wider claims require additional work. The paragraph's intellectual contribution lies partly in making those boundaries available to scrutiny.",
            sq("What do both shortcut readings fail to preserve?", "Support for the account alongside limits on its reach", "A claim that no cases were observed", "An unrestricted conclusion endorsed by the authors", "Corroboration desteği artırır; caveat kapsamı sınırlar. İkisi birlikte ele alınmalıdır."),
            sq("What specifically limits wider applicability?", "Selection from institutions already interested in reform", "A complete absence of findings", "Identical participation by every institution", "Seçilmiş kurumların özelliği, daha geniş ortama genellemeyi sınırlar."),
            "The evidence supports the account in these cases, while its applicability elsewhere remains open.",
            sq("Which response is proportional?", "Retain the support and investigate the wider scope.", "Declare every observation invalid.", "Claim unrestricted applicability is proven.", "While, yerel destek ile açık kalan kapsamı aynı anda korur.")),
        s(6, "I was, of course, the only person who remained calm. That is why I raised my voice: someone had to restore order. Lina looked at the broken cup but said nothing, a silence I took as agreement. In the corridor later, I heard her telling a colleague that the meeting had frightened her. She must have meant the weather; the storm had been dreadful. The passage invites the reader to notice a gap between the narrator's self-description and the details he reports. His explanations repeatedly protect his image, even when the evidence points elsewhere. Lina's silence is assigned a meaning convenient to him, and her later statement is reinterpreted to avoid contradiction. The narrative does not require a reader to know every external fact to recognise this pattern of motivated interpretation and question the authority of his account.",
            sq("What most strongly supports doubting the narrator's interpretation?", "He redirects contrary evidence to protect his self-image.", "He supplies no details of the meeting at all.", "Lina explicitly confirms his complete calmness.", "Raised voice, broken cup ve frightened, anlatıcının kendini koruyan açıklamalarıyla gerilim içindedir."),
            sq("How does he initially interpret Lina's silence?", "As agreement", "As an explicit accusation", "As proof she was absent", "A silence I took as agreement, yorumun anlatıcı tarafından atandığını belirtir."),
            "The narrator calls himself impartial, then dismisses every conflicting account without examining it.",
            sq("What does this pattern warrant?", "Questioning the narrator's claimed impartiality", "Accepting impartiality solely because he claims it", "Concluding that every reported event is invented", "Tutarlılık sorunu güvenilirliği sorgulatır; bütün olayların uydurma olduğunu tek başına kanıtlamaz.")),
        s(7, "The negotiators reached a deadlock not because no compromise was imaginable, but because each side feared how a concession would be presented to its own supporters. The mediator proposed separating a public statement of shared aims from the confidential discussion of implementation. This created room to explore options, yet raised a further concern: a shared statement must not imply agreement on details still contested. The parties therefore approved wording that named the common objective and explicitly reserved the unresolved terms. Progress depended on allowing movement without manufacturing consensus. A superficially triumphant announcement might have broken the deadlock for a day while undermining the trust needed to complete the work. The episode shows how audience, face and precision interact in negotiation, and why ambiguity can facilitate discussion only up to the point at which it begins to misrepresent commitment.",
            sq("What boundary does the approved statement preserve?", "Shared aims versus unresolved implementation terms", "Complete agreement on all disputed details", "An absence of any common objective", "Common objective korunurken unresolved terms açıkça saklı tutulur."),
            sq("Why could a triumphant announcement be damaging?", "It could manufacture consensus and undermine later trust.", "It would necessarily resolve every detail.", "It would remove all audiences from the negotiation.", "Manufacturing consensus, gerçekte olmayan taahhüt izlenimiyle güveni zedeler."),
            "We agree on the objective, but the statement explicitly leaves the timetable unresolved.",
            sq("Which claim would overstate the agreement?", "The parties have settled the timetable.", "The objective is shared.", "The timetable remains open.", "Explicitly unresolved takvim için anlaşma ilanını desteklemez.")),
        s(8, "When the lift failed for the fourth time that week, the caretaker announced that the building was offering residents an excellent opportunity to improve their fitness. His expression remained perfectly serious. Nobody understood this as the official purpose of the broken lift: the mismatch between the inconvenience and the cheerful benefit created the joke. A resident replied that the opportunity was becoming rather comprehensive, since the stairs now came with a leaking ceiling as well. The exchange uses deadpan delivery and understatement to communicate frustration without spelling it out. Its humour depends on shared recognition of the conditions; taken out of context, the positive phrases could be mistaken for genuine praise. Interpreting the tone therefore requires attending to the factual setting and the disproportion between that setting and the language, rather than relying on a smile or an explicit announcement that a joke is being made.",
            sq("What creates the humour in the caretaker's remark?", "A serious delivery of a benefit mismatched with repeated failure", "A literal claim that the lift was built for exercise", "An explicit statement that all residents enjoy leaks", "Tekrarlanan arızanın olumlu fırsat gibi sunulması ve deadpan ton uyumsuzluğu mizah yaratır."),
            sq("What does 'rather comprehensive' imply in context?", "The inconveniences are accumulating.", "The building is being praised without reservation.", "Only one minor benefit has appeared.", "Leaking ceiling eklenince understatement, çoğalan sorunları örtük eleştirir."),
            "After another outage, someone says, 'A remarkably reliable service,' in a deliberately flat voice.",
            sq("What most supports an ironic reading?", "The contrast between repeated outages and praise", "The word service alone", "Proof that no outage occurred", "Tekrarlanan kesintiyle reliable övgüsü arasında açık karşıtlık vardır.")),
        s(9, "The fictional notice stated that applications received after the specified date would not be considered, notwithstanding any earlier indication of interest. Readers unfamiliar with the register sometimes understood notwithstanding as introducing an exception that allowed late applications. In this sentence it does the reverse: an earlier indication does not override the stated deadline. A plain-language version therefore needed to preserve the relationship, not merely replace individual words with shorter ones. It explained that expressing interest earlier would not make a late application acceptable. The exercise concerns interpretation of an example notice, not the legal validity of an actual document. Its difficulty lies in tracking the scope of the qualification and resisting the temptation to infer a favourable exception from a formal connector whose function is concessive.",
            sq("What effect does the earlier indication of interest have in the example?", "It does not override the deadline.", "It guarantees acceptance of late applications.", "It cancels the specified date.", "Notwithstanding = buna rağmen; daha önce ilgi bildirmek geç başvuruyu kabul ettirmez."),
            sq("What must a plain-language version preserve?", "The relationship between the deadline and the qualification", "Only the original word count", "A favourable exception not present in the sentence", "Sözcük değişimi yetmez; istisna ilişkisi doğru korunmalıdır."),
            "The example says the rule applies notwithstanding prior approval of a draft.",
            sq("What is the intended relation?", "Prior draft approval does not displace the rule.", "Draft approval automatically cancels the rule.", "The rule has no stated scope.", "Concessive connector, önceki taslak onayına rağmen kuralın uygulandığını belirtir.")),
        s(10, "The study's abstract reported that the effect persisted after adjustment for several measured variables. The discussion was more guarded: an unmeasured factor could still account for part of the association, and replication in a different setting was needed. A reader who converted adjusted association into proven mechanism would move beyond the authors' claim. Equally, the possibility of residual confounding would not justify saying that the observed pattern did not exist. The task is to hold observation, statistical adjustment and causal explanation apart while examining how they relate. Dense prose can compress these distinctions into a few technical phrases, but those phrases should not be treated as ceremonial assurances. Their value lies in specifying what the analysis has addressed, what it has not addressed, and which alternative explanations remain live.",
            sq("Which reading exceeds the authors' claim?", "A mechanism has been proven conclusively.", "Measured variables were adjusted for.", "Replication in another setting is needed.", "Adjusted association, proven mechanism demek değildir; metin alternatif etkenleri açık bırakır."),
            sq("What does possible residual confounding not justify?", "Denying that the observed pattern existed", "Questioning a causal interpretation", "Seeking replication", "Gözlenen örüntünün varlığı ile nedensel açıklamanın kesinliği ayrılır."),
            "The association survives measured adjustments, but unmeasured influences may remain.",
            sq("Which conclusion respects the distinction?", "Adjustment strengthens the analysis without proving a unique cause.", "All possible causes have been eliminated.", "No association was observed.", "Measured adjustments, ölçülmemiş etkenleri otomatik ortadan kaldırmaz.")),
        s(11, "The editorial called the policy a common-sense correction and described its critics as defenders of an outdated privilege. Before any evidence was weighed, these labels distributed reasonableness between the sides. The article later quoted a critic, but only to illustrate resistance, not to examine the practical objection she raised. A critical analysis can identify this framing without assuming that the policy is therefore wrong. The relevant question is how the argument makes one position appear self-evident and the other suspect, and whether the supporting evidence independently sustains that division. A balanced paraphrase would strip away the presumption while preserving the substantive claim and the critic's objection. It would not manufacture equal evidential strength where none had been shown; it would make the construction of authority available for examination.",
            sq("What do the opening labels do?", "Assign reasonableness before the evidence is examined", "Provide a neutral measurement of outcomes", "Guarantee equal treatment of the objection", "Common-sense ve outdated privilege, tarafları kanıt öncesinde değerlendiren çerçevedir."),
            sq("What does a balanced paraphrase not require?", "Inventing equal evidential strength", "Preserving the substantive objection", "Removing unsupported presumptions", "Denge, kanıtlar eşitmiş gibi uydurmak değil; varsayımları görünür kılmaktır."),
            "The article labels one side sensible before discussing either side's evidence.",
            sq("What should analysis examine?", "How the label pre-allocates credibility", "Whether the label proves the conclusion", "Only the headline's length", "Önceden verilen sensible etiketi, güvenilirliği daha kanıt tartışılmadan dağıtır.")),
        s(12, "The chair celebrated the narrow vote as a victory, while a colleague called it Pyrrhic. The latter did not deny that the motion had passed; she pointed to the damaged alliance and the resources spent securing a decision that would now be difficult to implement. Another member described the situation as a catch-22: implementation required trust, yet the process used to win approval had weakened the trust needed to proceed. Neither allusion supplies a literal measurement of the costs. Each compresses a judgement about the relationship between success and its conditions. Understanding the passage requires keeping the procedural result distinct from the speaker's assessment of its value. The references are useful only if the reader connects them to the stated consequences rather than treating their cultural resonance as proof that the judgement must be correct.",
            sq("What does calling the vote Pyrrhic suggest?", "The formal win may be outweighed by its costs.", "The motion definitely failed to pass.", "No resources were spent.", "Motion passed korunuyor; alliance damage ve kaynak maliyeti zaferin değerini sorgulatıyor."),
            sq("What circular difficulty does 'catch-22' describe here?", "Implementation needs trust that the approval process weakened.", "Approval was obtained without any need for implementation.", "Every participant had unlimited trust.", "Gerekli güvenin onay sürecinde zayıflatılması, uygulamanın koşulunu kendi süreciyle bozuyor."),
            "The proposal passes, but winning has exhausted the resources needed to carry it out.",
            sq("Which allusion best fits that assessment?", "A Pyrrhic victory", "An unqualified triumph", "A failure to win any vote", "Kazanımın gerçekleştirme kapasitesini tüketen ağır bedeli Pyrrhic victory anlamına uyar."))
    )
}
